      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(2x+1)^2&=(x+5)^2+(x+2)^2-2(x+5)(x+2)\\cos60^{\\circ}\\\\4x^2+4x+1&=x^2+7x+19\\\\3x^2-3x-18&=0\\\\3(x-3)(x+2)&=0\\\\x&=-2\\text{ or }3\\end{align*}$$\nFor $x=-2$, $AB=0$ and $BC=-3$, so this root is inadmissible. For $x=3$, the side lengths are $5$, $7$ and $8$, all positive.\nHence, $x=3$.",
